INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(352100, 0, 3521, 0, 0, 8, 'Zangarmarsh', 'Zangarmarsh is a vast wetland in western Outland, where mushrooms taller than any tree rise over still pools and glowing fungi light the gloom. Sporebats drift overhead, and the giants that wade through the bogs are themselves made of living fungus. When the druids of the Cenarion Expedition arrived, they expected to find only small pockets of life and instead found a thriving wilderness. Then they noticed that the water was falling, and the marsh has begun to wither. Many peoples share the land: the draenei of Telredor and the Kurenai of the Orebor Harborage, the Darkspear trolls of Zabra''jin and Swamprat Post, the peaceful sporelings of Sporeggar, savage tribes of Lost Ones, the Ango''rosh ogres, who are cutting down the mushroom forests of the north, and the naga, who hold the shores of the great lakes, keep a stronghold beneath Serpent Lake in Coilfang Reservoir and have attacked the druids since the day they arrived.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Zangarmarsh (giant mushrooms, Vashj drains the marsh into Coilfang Reservoir, factions, Lost One tribes); quest 9716 description (expected small pockets of life, thriving ecosystem, water levels going down); quest 9718 reward text (pumping stations at all the major lakes); quest 9764 description (water redirected into Coilfang Reservoir); npc_text 9259 (mushrooms taller than trees); quest 9835 (Ango''rosh cleared the Hewn Bog); DB spawns: Sporebat, Fungal Giant, Bog Lord; quest 9728 description (naga attacks since the Expedition set foot in the marsh); quest 9729 reward text (the naga''s reservoir)'),
(352101, 1, 3521, 0, 0, 8, 'Cenarion Refuge', 'The Cenarion Refuge stands in the east of the marsh, at the end of the road from Hellfire Peninsula, and is the headquarters of the Cenarion Expedition. Its leader, Ysiel Windsinger, keeps watch from a balcony behind the inn, while Warden Hamoot and his wardens guard against the naga, who have attacked the druids since the day they arrived. Two great ancients, Ashyen, an Ancient of Lore, and Keleth, an Ancient of War, stand among the buildings and bless those the Expedition trusts. Lauranna Thar''well catalogues the marsh''s plants, the Broken refugee Ikeyen teaches the druids what he knows of the land, and Morthis Whisperwing waits for a worthy apprentice while his two birds, Rook and Corvax, circle overhead.', 'quest 9912 description (main path west from Cenarion Post leads to the refuge in eastern Zangarmarsh); quest 9718 description (balcony near Ysiel); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ysiel_Windsinger (back porch of the inn); quest 9728 description (naga attacks since we set foot here); creature_template subnames 17900 Ancient of Lore, 17901 Ancient of War; quest 9785; quest 9802 (Lauranna, cataloguer); npc_text 9131 (Ikeyen teaches the druids); npc_text 10735 (Morthis, Rook and Corvax); DB spawns in area 3565: 17841, 17858, 17900, 17901, 17909, 17956, 22832, 22842, 22843'),
(352102, 1, 3521, 1, 0, 8, 'Umbrafen Lake and Darkcrest Shore', 'Umbrafen Lake lies southwest of the Cenarion Refuge. On Darkcrest Shore the naga work a great steam pump, guarded by Darkcrest slavers and sorceresses who drive Dreghood Broken as drudges, and the pump''s overseer threatens intruders with the wrath of Warlord Kalithresh. The lake itself is home to Umbrafen eels, whose meat is a staple of the draenei at Telredor, and to mire hydras, whose thick scales resist the damp of the marsh.', 'quest 9716 description and reward text (Umbrafen Lake southwest of the refuge, steam pump, naga); quest 9720 (Umbrafen Lake pump controls); DB spawns: area 3841 Darkcrest Slaver 19946, Darkcrest Sorceress 19947, Dreghood Drudge 18122, Steam Pump Overseer 18340, Umbrafen Steam Pump Credit Marker 17998; area 3655 Umbrafen Eel, Mire Hydra; creature_text 18340 (Warlord Kalithresh will hear of this insolence); quest 9780 (Umbrafen eel a staple); quest 9774 (hydra scales stand up to dampness)'),
(352103, 1, 3521, 2, 0, 8, 'Umbrafen Village', 'South of the Cenarion Refuge lies Umbrafen Village, home of the Umbrafen, a tribe of Lost Ones who took the side of the naga. The Broken who escaped them call the Umbrafen the worst of all the traitor tribes: their oracles, seers and witchdoctors use dark magic to trap and enslave others, and they are especially cruel to slaves who flee. Their leader is Kataru. Those taken here are not easily freed. The druid Kayra Longmane was seized by a band of them while gathering herbs nearby, and Ikeyen of the Refuge still fears that they will come for him.', 'quest 9747 description (traitor tribes, dark magic, enslave, cruel to escaped slaves, Kataru, south of the refuge); quest 9752 description (Kayra abducted while gathering herbs); DB spawns in area 3641: Umbrafen Oracle 18077, Seer 18079, Witchdoctor 20115, Kataru 18080, Kayra Longmane 17969'),
(352104, 1, 3521, 3, 0, 8, 'Funggor Cavern', 'Funggor Cavern opens in the far south of the marsh, near the border with Nagrand and south of Umbrafen Village. It is the home of the sporeloks, who have lately been overrun by marsh dredgers and marsh lurkers that have invaded their caves. The Expedition sent watchers to study the cavern, but had to recall them after repeated attacks by the marsh beasts, and Warden Hamoot believes that killing their leader, Lord Klaq, would put an end to it. The Broken Ikeyen hid here after escaping the Umbrafen, only to flee again when the beasts and spore men fought over the cave, leaving behind everything he owned.', 'quest 10096 description (sporeloks live in Funggor Cavern, marsh beasts invaded, Ikeyen''s stories); quest 9894 description (watchers recalled from Funggor Cavern to the south, Lord Klaq); quest 9788 description and completion text (cave south of Umbrafen near the Nagrand border, marsh beasts and spore men); DB spawns in area 3652: Sporelok 18912, Marsh Lurker 18136, Marsh Dredger 18137; vmaps Md_Mushroomcave09B.wmo (WMO 4822) groups 22270/22271 -> 3652 in WMOAreaTable.dbc; gameobject 182122 Ikeyen''s Belongings inside'),
(352105, 1, 3521, 4, 0, 8, 'Telredor', 'Telredor is built atop a giant mushroom in the east of the marsh, its halls lit by cultivated fulgor spores, since little in the swamp will burn. For centuries it was a secluded retreat for draenei priests and pilgrims who seldom saw visitors. When the orcs began attacking the draenei, refugees arrived in growing numbers, and Anchorite Ahuurn and the other priests turned the shrine into a haven to which many owe their lives. Today it is the Alliance''s stronghold in the marsh. Vindicator Idaar watches over the land, Noraani and Haalrun, once its only outsiders, help feed the newcomers, and a dwarf of the Explorers'' League has come to settle a score with a giant wasp.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Telredor (built on a giant mushroom, draenei stronghold); quest 9777 description (little will burn, fulgor mushrooms for light); npc_text 9261 (secluded retreat, refugees, Ahuurn turned it into a safe haven); quest 9780 description (Noraani and Haalrun the only outsiders); quest 9896 description (Prospector Conall, Blacksting); DB spawns in area 3644: 18003, 18004, 18005, 18006, 18295; zone_npcs map coordinates (Telredor NPCs about 68,49)'),
(352106, 1, 3521, 5, 0, 8, 'The Dead Mire', 'The Dead Mire, northeast of Telredor, is a stretch of cracked and parched ground where the marsh has dried away, and almost everything living on it withers. Withered giants stalk it, attacking anything in their path, while parched hydras and withered bog lords roam the baked mud. Threshalisks lie in the dirt playing dead before they charge, and pieces of steam pumps lie scattered about. No one who has ventured in has ever reported seeing anything alive and well there.', 'quest 9782 description (land to the northeast of Telredor withering); quest 9783 description (soil devoid of moisture, giants driven mad); quest 9827 and 9828 reward text (once a lake, spawning ground, cannot spore); quest 10355 (parched hydra, withered bog lords); creature_text 19706 (Marshrock Threshalisk stops playing dead); DB: 43+ Steam Pump Part gameobjects 181871 in area 3648; quests 9771, 9772 (Scout Jyoba, inkwell, withered giant); DB spawns in area 3648: Withered Giant 18124, Withered Bog Lord 19402, Parched Hydra 20324, Scout Jyoba 18035'),
(352107, 1, 3521, 6, 0, 8, 'Swamprat Post', 'Swamprat Post is the Horde''s newest outpost in the marsh, raised by Darkspear trolls just south of the Dead Mire. Shadow Hunter Denjai sent Zurai there with a small band of builders and warriors to give the Horde a presence on the eastern border, after the Alliance began fortifying old draenei ruins, and to tighten the Horde''s hold on the roads in and out of the marsh. Marshfang rippers are everywhere, mail armor soon fails in the damp, and the cook answers every complaint of hunger by handing over an axe and pointing at a mushroom. Meanwhile Reavij pines for Magasha, Magasha has eyes only for Zurai, and the witch doctor''s charms have done nothing to change that.', 'quest 10103 description (Alliance militarizing draenei ruins, trolls built a new outpost south of the Dead Mire); npc_text 9267 (Zurai, builders and warriors); quest 9775 reward text (presence on the eastern border); quest 10105 description (control of the roads in and out of the marsh); quest 9770 (marshfang rippers); quest 9774 (mail armor useless in the swamp); quest 9773 (cook hands you an axe); quest 9898, npc_text 9268, 9269 (Reavij, Magasha, Zurai, Tor''gash''s charms)'),
(352108, 1, 3521, 7, 0, 8, 'Feralfen Village', 'Feralfen Village lies in the south central marsh, home of the Feralfen, said to be the most powerful tribe of Lost Ones in Zangarmarsh and keepers of potent medicine. Their mystics, hunters and druids have turned to the worship of animal spirits, and they carve idols and totems in honor of the spirits they revere. Just north of the village roams Blacksting, a giant bog wasp that drove off the first Explorers'' League party to camp there.', 'quest 9846 description (most powerful tribe, powerful medicine, mystics, hunters, druids); quest 9787 description and reward text (animal spirits, birds, none native, arakkoa); quest 9846 reward text (serpent and bird spirit); quest 9896 description (Blacksting, camped just north of the Feralfen Village); DB spawns in area 3642: Feralfen Hunter 18113, Mystic 18114, Druid 20270, Feralfen Idol 182139, Blacksting 18283'),
(352109, 1, 3521, 8, 0, 8, 'Boha''mu Ruins', 'The Boha''mu Ruins are the remains of a draenei temple southwest of Telredor, one of several shrines once kept by a small order of anchorites and vindicators. Contact with its keepers was lost during the orcs'' war on the draenei, and the Feralfen Lost Ones have since made the ruins their own. Their elder, Kuruti, dwells in the temple itself, and the tribe''s mystics and hunters walk its old stones.', 'quest 9786 description and reward text (Boha''mu temple southwest of Telredor, shrines, lost contact, Feralfen remember their heritage); npc_text 9227, 9231 (Kuruti: my temple, leave in peace); quest 9847 description and reward text (totem at the foot of the stairs, spirit attacked); DB spawn: Elder Kuruti 18197 in area 3668'),
(352110, 1, 3521, 9, 0, 8, 'The Lagoon and Darkcrest Enclave', 'The Lagoon lies in the south central marsh, a broad stretch of water haunted by lagoon eels, mire hydras and lagoon walkers, among them a great one called Marsh Baron Brok. On its shore stands the Darkcrest Enclave, where the naga run another of their steam pumps. Darkcrest taskmasters and sirens keep Dreghood Broken at the work, and the enclave answers to Rajah Haghazed, leader of the Darkcrest naga. The Cenarion Expedition has tied the Darkcrest to many attacks on its people, and a bounty posted at the Refuge warns that the rajah is extremely dangerous.', 'quest 9730 description (Rajah Haghazed, leader of the Darkcrest, at the Lagoon in the central southern region, numerous attacks, extremely dangerous); quest 9720 (Lagoon pump); DB spawns: area 3659 Lagoon Eel 20290, Mire Hydra 18213, Lagoon Walker 20291, Marsh Baron Brok 20292; area 3819 Darkcrest Taskmaster 18086, Siren 18087, Dreghood Drudge 18122, Rajah Haghazed 18046, Lagoon Steam Pump Credit Marker 17999'),
(352111, 1, 3521, 10, 0, 8, 'Cenarion Watchpost', 'The Cenarion Watchpost is a small camp in the southwest of the marsh, west of Quagg Ridge, where Watcher Leesa''oh studies the sporelings and bog lords. She believes that all things in nature are bound in one web, and that anyone who interferes without understanding it will surely cause destruction, so she prefers to watch quietly and take notes. Her fellow druids call her a bit studious. She is never alone: her big cat, Buddy, shares the camp and likes to scratch now and then, though she insists he is only a lovable kitty.', 'quest 9697 description (western region toward the south, studious, watch out for her cat); quest 9911 description (camp to the west of Quagg Ridge); npc_text 9128 (interconnected web, observe); npc_text 9085 (Buddy); DB spawns in area 3895: Watcher Leesa''oh 17831, Buddy 17953'),
(352112, 1, 3521, 11, 0, 8, 'Quagg Ridge', 'Quagg Ridge, east of the Cenarion Watchpost, is the land of the bog lords and fungal giants, towering creatures of living fungus. Many of them are starving. Lately they have been crossing the road to the Spawning Glen to devour the sporelings'' spore sacs, and husked mushroom remains lie discarded across the ridge. The sporelings have always kept the bog lords at bay with spears and stones, but the giants have grown more aggressive, or more desperate, and no longer fear them.', 'quest 9702 description (Quagg Ridge to the east, crossing the road, starving); quest 9701 reward text (bog lords of Quagg Ridge eating pods); quest 9702 reward text (husked mushroom remains); quest 9743 description (spears and stones, more aggressive or desperate); DB spawns in area 3646: Bog Lord 18127, Fungal Giant 19734, Starving Fungal Giant 18125, Starving Bog Lord 19519, Discarded Nutriment 182256'),
(352113, 1, 3521, 12, 0, 8, 'The Spawning Glen', 'The Spawning Glen, west of the Cenarion Watchpost, is where young sporelings come from. Their spore sacs grow here, starting large and shrinking as the air inside them is spent, until only small, mature sacs remain. It is a fragile nursery, and it is under attack: starving fungal giants and bog lords wander through the glen devouring the sacs. The sporeling Fahssn keeps a desperate watch over them and begs any friendly outsider who passes to save as many as can be saved.', 'quest 9701 description (Spawning Glen to the west of the watchpost); quest 9739 description and reward text (spore sacs, young come from here, fungal giants devouring); DB spawns in area 3647: Sporeggar Spawn 18358, Starving Fungal Giant 18125, Starving Bog Lord 19519, Mature Spore Sac 182069; quest 9739 log (Fahssn at the Spawning Glen)'),
(352114, 1, 3521, 13, 0, 8, 'Sporeggar', 'Sporeggar is the village of the sporelings, a small and mostly peaceful people, on the western side of Zangarmarsh between Sporewind Lake and Marshlight Lake. It is grown from tallstalk mushrooms raised from fertile spores, and much of it has had to be regrown after attacks by the bog lords. Glowcap mushrooms serve the sporelings as coin. Their elder, Msshi''fn, welcomes outsiders who prove themselves, though others, like Gshaff, still cannot decide what to make of them. The village has enemies on every side: the bog lords, the marsh walkers of old, the spore giants of the Underbog and the Bloodscale naga to the northeast.', 'quest 10945 description (west side of Zangarmarsh between the Sporewind and Marshlight lakes); quest 9806 description and reward text (tallstalks to rebuild after bog lord attacks); quest 9808 description (glowcaps as currency); npc_text 9202, 9201; quest 9719 (marsh walkers the historic danger); quest 9717 (war with the spore giants); quest 9726 (Bloodscale to the northeast); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Sporeggar (mostly peaceful race)'),
(352115, 1, 3521, 14, 0, 8, 'Marshlight Lake and Bloodscale Enclave', 'Marshlight Lake, in the west of the marsh, is the haunt of bogstroks, whose hatchlings swarm the shallows, and of a giant among them called Terrorclaw. On its shore the Bloodscale naga keep the Bloodscale Enclave and the Marshlight steam pump, worked by Wrekt slaves under the whips of slavedrivers and enchantresses. One naga taskmaster is said to amuse himself by sending slaves out to the lake''s islands just when Terrorclaw is ready to feed, and the enclave''s naga have also been killing the sporelings of nearby Sporeggar.', 'quest 9902 description (taskmaster sends slaves to the islands of Marshlight Lake when Terrorclaw is ready to feed); quest 9904 (Terrorclaw, giant bogstrok); quest 9729 description and reward text (Marshlight steam pump, Ark of Ssslith, most prized possession); quest 9726 (Bloodscale Enclave killing sporelings); DB spawns: area 3643 Bloodscale Slavedriver 18089, Enchantress 18088, Wrekt Slave 18123, Marshlight Steam Pump Credit Marker 18002; area 3656 Bogstrok Crusher, Razorclaw, Hatchling, Terrorclaw 20477; quest 9902 (Marshlight Lake southwest of Orebor)'),
(352116, 1, 3521, 15, 0, 8, 'Zabra''jin', 'Zabra''jin is the Darkspear town in the west of the marsh, overseen by Shadow Hunter Denjai, who commands the trolls'' forces in Zangarmarsh. Witch Doctor Tor''gash reads omens in burstcap spores and keeps two pet murlocs, Gargle and Gurgle, while Seer Janidi says he need only ask the spirits. Gambarinka has given up rusting metal tools for the blades of marshfang slicers, Zurjaya is glad of fishing water after the wastes of Hellfire, and a captured gnome repairs gear under a guard who threatens to eat him. Yet the town is hemmed in by ogres cutting their way from the north and Daggerfen assassins on the roads, and a messenger from Garadar has come begging for help.', 'npc_text 9248 (Denjai, commander of the Darkspear forces); quest 9814 (burstcap omens); quest 9816 (Gargle and Gurgle); npc_text 9250 (Janidi on Tor''gash); quest 9842 (Gambarinka''s blades); quest 9845 (Zurjaya after Hellfire); creature_text 19380 (Guard Untula), creature 19383 Captured Gnome <Item Repair>; quest 9820, 10118 (ogres, Daggerfen); quest 9797 description (Messenger Gazgrigg, Garadar must not fall); DB spawns in area 3645: 18013, 18014, 18015, 18017, 18018, 18091, 18150, 18151, 19380, 19383'),
(352117, 1, 3521, 16, 0, 8, 'Daggerfen Village', 'Daggerfen Village lies in the northwest of the marsh, west of the Orebor Harborage. Its people, the Daggerfen, are the most cunning and aggressive of the marsh''s Lost One tribes, a whole tribe of assassins who brew a potent poison from a ragveil base. They make no secret of wanting to rule the other Lost Ones, and under Chieftain Mummaki they have killed many scouts and messengers, Kurenai, draenei and troll alike, in a bid to seize the roads. Not everything here is grim: a few baby murlocs splash among the huts, though the marsh is said to have no murlocs of its own.', 'quest 10118 description (most cunning and aggressive, desire control over other Lost Ones, roads); quest 9848 description and reward text (tribe of assassins, poison, ragveil base); quests 10116, 10117 (Mummaki, attacks on Orebor and Zabra''jin, west of Orebor, northwest of Zabra''jin); quest 9816 (Tor''gash''s murloc gift); DB spawns in area 3640: Daggerfen Muckdweller 18115, Assassin 18116, Chieftain Mummaki 19174, Baby Murloc 18152, Daggerfen Poison Manual 182184; quest 9816 description (there be no murlocs here)'),
(352118, 1, 3521, 17, 0, 8, 'Hewn Bog', 'The Hewn Bog, in the north of the marsh, has earned its name. Ango''rosh ogres have moved in and are chopping down its giant mushrooms, a cutting operation overseen by the brute Boss Grog''ak, and the felling threatens to cut a path to the walls of Zabra''jin. Ogres and their shamans now swarm where the mushroom forest stood, and the Kurenai of the Orebor Harborage watch them draw ever closer to their temple.', 'quest 9708 description and reward text (Hewn Bog to the north, ogres moved in, explains everything); quest 9820 description (Boss Grog''ak, mushroom-cutting operation north of Zabra''jin); quest 9835 description (cleared the Hewn Bog of its towering mushrooms); DB spawns in area 3667: Ango''rosh Ogre 18117, Ango''rosh Shaman 18118, Boss Grog''ak 18159; quest 9835 description (cleared the Hewn Bog, draw ever closer to our refuge)'),
(352119, 1, 3521, 18, 0, 8, 'Ango''rosh Grounds and Stronghold', 'Northwest of Zabra''jin, the Ango''rosh ogres hold lands of their own. The Ango''rosh Grounds are an armed camp of brutes, maulers, warlocks and sentries under Captain Krosh and Captain Bo''kar. Beyond the camp, a fallen mushroom bridges the water to a small floating island, and in a cave there lies the Ango''rosh Stronghold, stacked with boxes of harvested mushrooms and held by maulers, souleaters, shadowmages and Mal''druk the Soulrender. Its master is Overlord Gorefist, the leader who holds the whole tribe together.', 'quest 9822 description and reward text (Ango''rosh Grounds to the northwest, attack plans); quests 9823, 9839, 9709 (cave on a small island, fallen mushroom bridge, floating island, boxes of mushrooms); quest 9839 description (leader is the centerpiece of the tribe); DB spawns: area 3650 Ango''rosh Sentry, Brute, Warlock, Mauler, Captain Krosh 18992, Captain Bo''kar 20442, Attack Plans 182166; area 3651 Mauler, Souleater, Shadowmage, Box of Mushrooms 182050, Overlord Gorefist 18160, Mal''druk the Soulrender 20445'),
(352120, 1, 3521, 19, 0, 8, 'Orebor Harborage', 'In the ruins of an old draenei temple northwest of Serpent Lake, a small band of Broken has made a home. These are the Kurenai, Broken who wish to reunite with their draenei kin, sent from their city of Telaar in Nagrand under Ikuti to strengthen ties with Telredor and keep the roads between them open. They are wary of strangers, for wariness has kept them alive. Puluu senses that the temple once meant something to him and hopes the draenei can help him remember. Maktu makes armor of fenclaw hide, and a human who likes to be called the specialist studies the poisons of the Lost Ones.', 'quest 9776 description and reward text (ruins of an old temple northwest of Serpent Lake, wariness); quest 9835 description (Kurenai, mission from Nagrand, ties to Telredor); quest 9833 description (Telaar the Kurenai home city, roads); npc_text 9237 (Puluu''s memories); quests 9834, 9902 reward text (Maktu''s armor, once a slave); npc_text 9238, quest 9848 (Timothy Daniels the specialist); DB spawns in area 3766: 18008, 18009, 18010, 18019; CreatureDisplayInfo 17422 (HumanMale) for Timothy Daniels'),
(352121, 1, 3521, 20, 0, 8, 'Serpent Lake and Bloodscale Grounds', 'Serpent Lake spreads across the north of the marsh. On its eastern shore the Bloodscale naga hold the Bloodscale Grounds and the lake''s own steam pump, where overseers, wavecallers and elementals drive Wrekt slaves under the command of the sorceress Rajis Fyashe. The deep water belongs to fenclaw thrashers, swarms of mudfin frenzies and Mragesh, an old and cunning hydra that has dogged many an angler and once nearly made a meal of a Kurenai hunter.', 'quest 9731 description and reward text (drains and pumps connect the lakes to Serpent Lake, giant drain in the center, water sink); quest 9817 description (Rajis Fyashe, naga sorceress, Serpent Lake in the north); quests 9903, 9905 (Mragesh, cunning, dogged anglers, attacked Maktu); quest 9845 (fenclaw thrashers); DB spawns: area 3818 Bloodscale Overseer 20088, Wavecaller 20089, Bloodscale Elemental 20792, Wrekt Slave 18123, Rajis Fyashe 18044, Serpent Steam Pump Credit Marker 18000; area 3653 Mudfin Frenzy, Fenclaw Thrasher, Mragesh 18286; creature spawns mapped: Bloodscale Overseer x 59-66, Mudfin Frenzy x 39-60'),
(352122, 1, 3521, 21, 0, 8, 'Coilfang Reservoir', 'Beneath Serpent Lake, reached through the water, lies Coilfang Reservoir, the stronghold of the naga of the marsh. In its great cavern stone archways lead to the slave pens, the Underbog and the steam vaults, where Warlord Kalithresh is said to command, and deeper still to the Serpentshrine Cavern. At the entrance, Watcher Jhang of the Expedition waits with a twisted ankle for word of four companions who went on inside, and Mortog Steamhead, saved by the Expedition from certain death in the mines, trades with the Expedition''s friends.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Coilfang_Reservoir (beneath Serpent Lake, pumping station, entered underwater, four wings ending with Lady Vashj); quest 9764 description (orders: slay druids on sight, double the water redirection); quest 9763 description (stone archway, steam vaults, Kalithresh); quest 9738 description (four companions in the Slave Pens and Underbog); npc_text 9112 (Jhang''s twisted ankle); npc_text 10936 (Mortog rescued from the mines); DB: Watcher Jhang 17884 and Mortog Steamhead 23373 stand in area 3653 by the instance portals; WMOAreaTable.dbc rows 39182/40930 (WMO 4630 group 21363 -> 3905); vmaps Coilfang_Zangarentrance.wmo spawn on map 530'),
(352123, 1, 3521, 22, 0, 8, 'Twin Spire Ruins', 'The Twin Spire Ruins stand near the middle of the marsh, the remains of a holy draenei site whose single broken tower, despite the name, still rises over an old burial ground. Both the Alliance and the Horde contest the surrounding marsh: each side strives to hold the two towers that watch over this part of Zangarmarsh and to raise its battle standard over the burial ground, and control passes back and forth as the fighting ebbs and flows. Around the ruins, mudfin frenzies thrash in the shallows and sporebats drift among the stones.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Twin_Spire_Ruins (holy draenei site, one ruined central tower, two towers flank the burial ground, battle standard); DB spawns in area 3720: Mudfin Frenzy 18212, Sporebat 18128, Spirit Healer 6491'),
(352124, 2, 3521, 0, 0, 8, 'Ysiel Windsinger', 'Ysiel Windsinger, a night elf druid, leads the Cenarion Expedition from the Cenarion Refuge. The Expedition began as a small venture of the Cenarion Circle, but it has since grown large and largely independent, though she has not forgotten that it cannot exist without the Circle''s support. She came to Outland expecting small pockets of life and found a thriving marsh, then watched its waters fall. Her magic can reshape a willing helper into a form suited to scouting the lakes from the air, and she means to learn why they are falling.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ysiel_Windsinger (night elf druid, leader); quest 9912 description (began small under the Circle, now large and autonomous); quest 9724 reward text (cannot exist without the Circle''s support); quest 9716 description; quest 9718 description (mold your shape for scouting); quest 9764 reward text, 9765 description (prepare for war, began as a peaceful venture); CreatureDisplayInfo 17275 (NightElfFemale)'),
(352125, 2, 3521, 1, 0, 8, 'Morthis Whisperwing', 'Morthis Whisperwing is a former member of the Druids of the Talon, the old order that taught young druids the mysteries of flight before the druidic orders came together as the Cenarion Circle. The order is no more, but Morthis means to remain one of them to the end of his days, and he has long searched for an apprentice worthy of the secrets of the stormcrow. He is proud and particular, and pollen makes him sneeze, to his great indignity. He envies the freedom of his two birds, Rook and Corvax, and says he will take wing again once one last task is done.', 'quest 10955 description and reward text (Druids of the Talon, dissolution, apprentice, remain one to the last of my days, secrets of the stormcrow); quest 10961 reward text (pollen, sneeze, indignity); npc_text 10735 (Rook and Corvax, on wing once more); creature_template 22832 subname Druid of the Talon, DB spawn area 3565'),
(352126, 2, 3521, 2, 0, 8, 'Warden Hamoot', 'Warden Hamoot is in charge of the Cenarion Expedition''s security. Ysiel brought wardens with her because she expected some opposition in Outland, but no one foresaw the strength and numbers of the naga, whose lethal attacks began the moment the Expedition set foot in the marsh. While the druids study plants and lakes, Hamoot deals with the hostiles. He pays out the Expedition''s bounties on the leaders of the Bloodscale and the Darkcrest, pays for proof of victories over the naga, and has set his sights on the marsh beasts of Funggor Cavern. He never liked the naga of Azeroth, likes these even less, and sheds no tears for them.', 'npc_text 9167 (wardens brought along, did not expect such strength or numbers); quest 9728 description and reward text (deal with hostiles, naga claws, more vicious than Azerothian ones); quests 9730, 9817 (bounties, rewards via Hamoot); quest 9894 (Hamoot and Lord Klaq); quest 9730 reward text (no tears for dead naga)'),
(352127, 2, 3521, 3, 0, 8, 'Ikeyen', 'Ikeyen is a Broken who escaped slavery among the Umbrafen Lost Ones and found safety at the Cenarion Refuge. The druids protect him from the naga and the traitor tribes, and in return he teaches them about the plants and animals of the marsh. Old and weakened, he has lived in fear of his former masters, certain that the Umbrafen would cut his throat if he left the Refuge for even a day. After his escape he hid in a cave south of their village, only to find it fought over by marsh beasts and spore men, and he had to flee again, leaving behind the few things he owned.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ikeyen (Broken, captured by the Umbrafen, escaped to the Refuge); npc_text 9131; quest 9747 description and reward text (escaped slaves, slit my throat, old and weakened); quest 9788 description; CreatureDisplayInfo 17767 (BrokenMale)'),
(352128, 2, 3521, 4, 1, 8, 'Anchorite Ahuurn', 'Anchorite Ahuurn leads Telredor. Once a cloistered priest of a quiet retreat, he opened its doors when the orcs fell upon his people and turned the shrine into a haven for refugees, and many draenei owe him their lives. He says Telredor has seen more change in twenty years than in the centuries before, and that the Light has brought him friends he could never have met in his cloister. He hopes to make Telredor a safe home for all who stand with the draenei, has reached out to the Kurenai at the Orebor Harborage, and longs to welcome even the Lost Ones of the marsh back among their people.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Telredor (Ahuurn the leader); npc_text 9265 (20 years of change, cloistered priest, the Light brought friends); npc_text 9261 (Idaar: Ahuurn transformed the shrine, many owe survival); quest 9776 description (safe haven for all allies, Orebor); quest 9803 reward text (Feralfen refused); quest 9803 description (welcome his people as our long lost brothers)'),
(352129, 2, 3521, 5, 1, 8, 'Ikuti', 'Ikuti leads the Kurenai at the Orebor Harborage, a band of Broken sent from Telaar in Nagrand to strengthen ties with the draenei of Telredor. He greets visitors kindly but admits that wariness has often been all that stood between his people and death, and his trust must be earned. The Kurenai are content to help the Lost Ones who seek them out, yet unlike some draenei they will not go chasing after the rest, though they act quickly against tribes like the Daggerfen. Those who prove themselves to Ikuti are sent on to Telaar with his word, to Nahuud.', 'npc_text 9235 (Ikuti of the Kurenai, not your enemies); quest 9776 reward text (wariness all that stands between my people and death); quest 9835 description (mission from Nagrand, ties to Telredor); quest 10115 description and reward text (Kurenai and draenei on the Lost Ones, Daggerfen); quest 9792 description and reward text (Nahuud at Telaar, like a brother)'),
(352130, 2, 3521, 6, 2, 8, 'Shadow Hunter Denjai', 'Shadow Hunter Denjai oversees Zabra''jin and commands the Darkspear forces in Zangarmarsh. He sent a crew east to build Swamprat Post and give the Horde a presence on the eastern border, and he expects regular reports, which some of his trolls find a trial. Denjai has reason to worry. The Ango''rosh ogres are cutting their way toward his walls, and he cannot believe the place they chose is an accident, while Daggerfen assassins pick off his scouts and messengers and threaten to surround the town. He means to send word north to the orcs of Thunderlord Stronghold, asking for any help they can spare.', 'npc_text 9248 (overseer of the outpost, commander of the Darkspear forces); npc_text 9267, quest 9775 (Zurai, reports, eastern border); quests 9820, 9822 (ogres, attack plans); quest 10118 description (Daggerfen, scouts and messengers, surrounded); quest 9795 description and reward text (Thunderlord Stronghold, Nekthar, ogres there too)'),
(352131, 2, 3521, 7, 0, 8, 'Msshi''fn', 'Msshi''fn is the elder of Sporeggar, called the Sporeggar Primus, and it falls to him to see that his people have what they need. He welcomes outsiders who prove their friendship, even though few of their kind ever come to Sporeggar, and he receives with gratitude the rescued spore sacs that carry the next generation of sporelings. Like the rest of his people he deals in glowcap mushrooms, which the sporelings use as coin, and he will teach a trusted friend how to pick them from the ground without ruining them.', 'creature_template 17924 subname Sporeggar Primus; quest 9809 reward text (as Sporeggar''s elder); npc_text 9202 (welcome, proven your worth); quest 9919 reward text (protected the next generation); quest 9808 description (glowcaps as currency, teach you to pick them)'),
(352132, 2, 3521, 8, 0, 8, 'Fhwoor', 'Fhwoor is a fungal giant who lives among the sporelings of Sporeggar, an odd sight given how much grief the other giants of the marsh cause them. He speaks simply. He likes the little sporelings, he says, because they saved him, and he does not eat them. He hates the naga and would dearly like to smash them, for the naga have been troubling his little friends, and that makes Fhwoor very angry.', 'npc_text 9113 (Fhwoor like little sporelings, they save Fhwoor, not eat them, hate naga, smash); quest 9729 description (little naga make Fhwoor angry, sporelings good friend); quest 9729 description and reward text (saved from the naga, stayed helping, ark, most prized possession); creature_text 17877'),
(352133, 2, 3521, 9, 0, 8, 'Rajis Fyashe', 'Rajis Fyashe is a naga found on the Bloodscale Grounds, on the eastern shore of Serpent Lake. Overseers and wavecallers stand about her, elementals move among them, and Wrekt slaves toil at the lake''s great steam pump under their eyes. She fights with frost and water, hurling bolts of ice, ringing her foes in freezing cold, raising spouts of water beneath them and calling elementals up at their feet, and when sorely wounded she flees to her guards for help. Few reach her without first cutting their way through the naga of the grounds.', 'quest 9817 description (leader of the Bloodscale, naga sorceress, Serpent Lake, extreme caution); quest 9817 completion and reward text (best news I''ve heard all day, attacks on expedition scouts); smart_scripts 18044 (Frostbolt 15043, Freezing Circle 34787, Water Spout 35499, Mass Elementals 35594, flee for assist at 15 percent); Spell.dbc descriptions (circle of ice that freezes enemies, elementals summoned at the feet of enemies); DB spawns: Rajis Fyashe 18044 in area 3818 with Bloodscale Overseer 20088, Wavecaller 20089, Bloodscale Elemental 20792, Wrekt Slave 18123, Serpent Steam Pump Credit Marker 18000'),
(352134, 3, 3521, 0, 0, 8, 'Balance Must Be Preserved', 'When the Cenarion Expedition came to Zangarmarsh, its druids expected to find small pockets of life in Outland and found a lush, thriving marsh instead. Their measurements soon told a darker story: the water in the lakes and marshes has been falling steadily ever since they began taking readings, and the impact on the plants and creatures of the marsh could be disastrous. Ysiel Windsinger means to find the cause before it is too late, and sends a helper southwest to Umbrafen Lake to search for clues to the water''s loss.', 'quest 9716 description and reward text; quest 9718 description and reward text (Stormcrow Amulet, pumping stations at all major lakes); quest 9720 description and reward text (Ironvine Seeds, rage of the earth, thick as your arm, strong as iron, saved for now)'),
(352135, 3, 3521, 1, 0, 8, 'The Drain Beneath Serpent Lake', 'Drain schematics carried by the Bloodscale naga and the overseers of the steam pumps show an underground system of drains and pumps linking the lakes of Zangarmarsh to Serpent Lake in the north. If the plans are right, a giant drain lies at the very center of the lake, hidden beneath its waters. They are worth confirming. Ysiel Windsinger, who leads the Cenarion Expedition''s study of the marsh''s falling waters from the Cenarion Refuge, will want to hear at once whether the drain is real, and what it could mean.', 'quest 9731 description and reward text (drain schematics, giant drain, water sink, team sent); quest 9724 description and reward text (emissaries in Hellfire Peninsula, Amythiel at Cenarion Post); quest 9732 description (affairs in Moonglade and Silithus); quest 9876 description and reward text (druids did not return, injuries); quest 9738 description (four companions in the Slave Pens and Underbog); quest 9763 description (archway, Kalithresh); quest 9764 description and reward text (Vashj''s seal, prepare for war); item 24330 Drain Schematics starts 9731, dropped by Bloodscale naga and Steam Pump Overseers'),
(352136, 3, 3521, 2, 0, 8, 'The Bog Lords'' Hunger', 'At the Cenarion Watchpost, Watcher Leesa''oh means to learn how the sporelings of Sporeggar live alongside the creatures around them. Her way is patient: watch quietly, take notes, and never interfere without understanding, for all things in nature are bound in one web. There is a great deal to do and she must stay at her camp to organize it, so she sends her helpers out into the field, beginning with a survey of the Spawning Glen to the west, where the young sporelings come from.', 'quest 9697 (Lethyn Moonfire sends help to Leesa''oh); quest 9701 description and reward text; quest 9702 description and reward text; quest 9708 description and reward text (Hewn Bog, ogres, every bit as much right); quest 9709 description and reward text (boxes of mushrooms, Ango''rosh Stronghold, new food supply); creature_text 17831 (Buddy, it''s working, saved both); npc_text 9128 (interconnected web, observe); quest 9697 reward text (so much to do, stay here to organize it)'),
(352137, 3, 3521, 3, 0, 8, 'The Sporelings'' Plight', 'At the Spawning Glen, the sporeling Fahssn begs passing strangers for help. Fungal giants are devouring the spore sacs from which young sporelings come. The sacs start out large and shrink as the air inside them is spent, and only the small, mature ones can be saved. The bog lords are worse. The sporelings have always kept them at bay with spears and stones, but lately the giants have grown more aggressive, or more desperate, and no longer fear sporeling weapons. Fahssn would be forever in the debt of anyone who fought them off.', 'quests 9739, 9743 descriptions and reward texts (Fahssn, spore sacs, spears and stones); quest 9919 description and reward text (to Msshi''fn, welcomed into homes, many questions); quest 9729 objectives and reward text (Fhwoor, Marshlight steam pump, Ark of Ssslith, most prized possession, we can do much worse, return to their reservoir, leave us in peace)'),
(352138, 3, 3521, 4, 0, 8, 'Spirits of the Feralfen', 'Anchorite Ahuurn of Telredor wants to know what has become of the old draenei shrines of the marsh. During the orcs'' war his people lost contact with the anchorites who kept them, among them the temple of Boha''mu to the southwest, and he has heard that a tribe of Lost Ones has settled there and may even be using the ruins. At Zabra''jin, Seer Janidi has his own interest in the same tribe. The Feralfen are said to be the most powerful Lost Ones in the marsh and to possess potent medicine, and Janidi wants their totems, for anything that might help him channel the spirits of this world cannot be ignored.', 'quest 9786 description and reward text; quest 9787 description and reward text (birds, arakkoa); quest 9801 description (potion of arakkoa form); quest 9803 description and reward text; npc_text 9227, 9229 (Kuruti: turned their backs on us, deception, no redemption); quests 9846, 9847 descriptions and reward texts (Janidi, serpent spirit, attacked)'),
(352139, 3, 3521, 5, 0, 8, 'The Withering of the Dead Mire', 'At Telredor, Vindicator Idaar has noticed a disturbing change in the land to the northeast: virtually all life there has begun to wither and die, seemingly without explanation, and he wants a sample of its soil to test his ideas. At Swamprat Post the trolls call the same place the Dead Mire. No one has ever reported seeing anything alive there, and Scout Jyoba, who volunteered to explore it, left three days ago and has not returned. Some who fight the withered giants carry away a strange, sickly basidium and wonder what it once did.', 'quest 9782 description and reward text; quest 9783 description and reward text; quests 9827 and 9828 descriptions and reward texts (withered basidium, once a lake, spawning ground); quest 10355 description and reward text; quests 9771, 9772 (Scout Jyoba, inkwell, report from the withered giants); item 24483/24484 Withered Basidium dropped by Withered Giant 18124'),
(352140, 3, 3521, 6, 0, 8, 'The Ango''rosh Threat', 'The Ango''rosh ogres are pressing on both sides of the marsh. At Zabra''jin a wanted poster calls for the head of Boss Grog''ak, overseer of the mushroom cutting north of the town, whose brutes are chopping a path toward its walls. At the Orebor Harborage, Ikuti of the Kurenai watches the same ogres strip the Hewn Bog of its towering mushrooms and creep ever closer to the old temple his people shelter in, and he asks any who would call themselves friends to fight them. The heart of the tribe lies in the Ango''rosh Stronghold, a cave on a small island beyond a fallen mushroom.', 'quest 9820 description and reward text (wanted poster, Grog''ak, filtering down from the northern mountains); quest 9822 description and reward text; quest 9823 description and reward text (stronghold, fallen mushroom bridge, another bloodthirsty chieftain); quest 9835 description (Hewn Bog cleared, temple); quest 9839 description and reward text (infighting to determine who will lead)'),
(352141, 3, 3521, 7, 0, 8, 'The Raven God', 'Before all the druidic orders came together as the Cenarion Circle, the Druids of the Talon taught promising young druids the mysteries of flight. The order is gone, and its former members teach the skill sparingly, but Morthis Whisperwing still searches for a suitable apprentice. Few druids have truly mastered all the forms open to them. Those who show the promise he requires are sent to him at the Cenarion Refuge in Zangarmarsh, to learn, if he finds them worthy, the secrets of the stormcrow.', 'quests 10955, 10961, 10964, 10978, 10979 descriptions and reward texts; quests 10980, 10990, 10991, 10992 (book of the raven, eagle, falcon, hawk essences); quest 10993 reward text (Anzu); quest 10994 description (Southfury moonstone, Azshara); quest 11001 description (Sethekk Halls, lure Anzu from the Emerald Dream); quest 11011 description; creature_text 22832 (Ward of Waking); quest 10965 description (fragment of Clintar''s spirit guides the search); creature_text 22924 (Book of the Raven, Anzu named); quest 10988 (raven stones buried near Skettis)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(352102, 1, 0, 255, 'It was here that the Cenarion Expedition first went looking for the cause of the falling water, and here that it found its first answer. The pump on Darkcrest Shore is drawing the lake away, and with that discovery the naga''s attacks on the druids at last made sense.', 'quest 9716 description and reward text (Umbrafen Lake, steam pump part of the cause, explains their open hostility)'),
(352106, 1, 0, 255, 'A troll scout from Swamprat Post, Jyoba, came here to explore and never returned. His body lies in the mire beside a spilled inkwell, his weapon still sheathed, and flecks of withered fungus on it suggest that one of the withered giants caught him by surprise as he sat writing his report.', 'quest 9771 description and reward text (inkwell, weapon sheathed, taken by surprise); quest 9772 description (offered on turning in 9771: flecks of withered fungus, withered giant); DB spawn: Scout Jyoba 18035 in area 3648'),
(352106, 2, 0, 255, 'The mire is drying out. Its ground has all but lost its moisture, everything on it is dried or wilting, and the lack of water has driven the fungal giants that live there berserk.', 'quest 9782 description, quest 9783 description (offered on turning in 9782: soil nearly devoid of moisture, withering giants driven mad); quest 9772 reward text (everything dried or wilting, giants berserk from the lack of moisture)'),
(352106, 3, 0, 255, 'The Dead Mire was once one of the marsh''s lakes, and the spawning ground of the fungal giants. With the water gone, the giants that remain can no longer spore, and if nothing changes they may disappear entirely.', 'quests 9827 and 9828 reward text (once a lake, spawning ground, cannot spore, may disappear entirely)'),
(352108, 1, 0, 255, 'The tribe''s carvings honor two spirits, a serpent and a bird. Seer Janidi of Zabra''jin, who studied the captured totems, scorns the bird as weak and capricious, but judges that the serpent wields considerable power.', 'quest 9846 reward text (serpent spirit and bird spirit, bird spirits weak and capricious, serpent wields considerable power)'),
(352108, 2, 0, 255, 'The idols show a fixation on birds, which is a puzzle, since no birds are native to Zangarmarsh. Anchorite Ahuurn of Telredor wonders whether the tribe once met the arakkoa, who to a shamanistic people might seem the very embodiment of a powerful bird spirit.', 'quest 9787 reward text (fixated on birds, none native, arakkoa)'),
(352109, 1, 0, 255, 'To the draenei of Telredor the Feralfen''s choice of home is a sign. They must remember something of their heritage and of what this place once meant, and Anchorite Ahuurn hopes the temple may hold the key to redeeming the Lost Ones and reuniting the many threads of the draenei.', 'quest 9786 reward text (they must remember something of their heritage, key to redeeming the Lost Ones)'),
(352109, 2, 0, 255, 'The tribe''s spirits guard the temple too. When a Darkspear seer had a totem planted below its stairs to summon the Feralfen serpent spirit, the spirit came, and it attacked: its loyalty lies with the Lost Ones.', 'quest 9847 description and reward text (totem at the foot of the stairs, the spirit attacked, higher affinity for those Lost Ones)'),
(352115, 1, 0, 255, 'The enclave has lost its greatest treasure. The Bloodscale kept their most prized possession here, the Ark of Ssslith, until Fhwoor, the fungal giant who lives among the sporelings, marched in and carried it off to Sporeggar, a warning that the sporelings could do far worse.', 'quest 9729 description and reward text (Marshlight steam pump, Ark of Ssslith, most prized possession, we can do much worse)'),
(352117, 1, 0, 255, 'The murlocs are a gift. Witch Doctor Tor''gash of Zabra''jin, who keeps two pet murlocs of his own, decided the marsh was missing them and had a cage of colorful young murlocs set loose by the village''s northeastern huts, and he hopes the little Lost Ones are enjoying them.', 'quest 9816 description and reward text (no murlocs here, gift o'' murlocs, northeastern cluster of huts); DB spawns: Baby Murloc 18152 x4 in area 3640'),
(352118, 1, 0, 255, 'The harm reaches farther than it seems. Mushrooms from the bog match the husks found discarded on Quagg Ridge: this is where the bog lords once came to feed. With their food cut down and carried off by the ogres, the starving giants have turned on the sporelings'' spawning grounds instead.', 'quest 9702 reward text (husked mushroom remains); quest 9708 description and reward text (match, ogres explain everything, bog lords no longer going there for food)'),
(352119, 1, 0, 255, 'The camp holds more than tents and weapons. Plans found here show the Ango''rosh making ready to fall on Zabra''jin, proof that their mushroom cutting so close to the troll town was no accident.', 'quest 9822 description and reward text (position no accident, attack plans, proof of their intentions)'),
(352120, 1, 0, 255, 'Maktu seldom speaks of it, but he was once a slave himself. Puluu, who has watched a naga taskmaster at Marshlight Lake send his slaves out to feed Terrorclaw, is ashamed that the Kurenai are too few to do more for their enslaved brethren, and hopes the draenei will one day help free the marsh of the naga.', 'quest 9902 description and reward text (taskmaster, Terrorclaw, too few, Maktu was once a slave)'),
(352121, 1, 0, 255, 'Serpent Lake lies at the heart of the naga''s design. Schematics taken from them show a hidden network of drains and pumps linking the lakes of the region to it, and at its center a giant drain swallows the water, making the lake a sink for all of Zangarmarsh.', 'quest 9731 description and reward text (drains and pumps connect the lakes to Serpent Lake, giant drain in the center, giant water sink)'),
(352122, 1, 0, 255, 'The druids Ysiel Windsinger sent to investigate the giant drain in Serpent Lake were expected back soon after, and they never returned. She has asked her most capable allies to look for them here, near the entrance to the reservoir beneath the lake, and to learn what became of them.', 'quest 9876 description and objectives (druids sent to investigate the drain inside Serpent Lake did not return, look for them near the entrance to Coilfang Reservoir)'),
(352124, 1, 0, 255, 'The first answer came from Umbrafen Lake: a steam pump worked by the naga was helping to drain the lake. Why they would do it, Ysiel could not say, but at last she understood their hostility toward her druids, and she wasted no time in finding out how widespread their work was.', 'quest 9716 reward text (the naga are behind this, but why, explains their open hostility, let''s not waste any time); quest 9718 description (offered on turning in 9716: how widespread the naga''s activity is)'),
(352127, 1, 0, 255, 'With Kataru and the Umbrafen seers, witchdoctors and oracles slain, Ikeyen says he will finally sleep comfortably at night. Were he not so old and weak, he would have dealt with his enemies himself, and though he has little to give, he insists that such kindness cannot go unpaid.', 'quest 9747 reward text (finally sleep comfortably, old and weakened, kindness cannot go unpaid)'),
(352128, 1, 0, 255, 'When he sent an envoy disguised as an arakkoa spirit to the Feralfen, they refused him. He grants that they may choose their own path, and that Elder Kuruti was right about the folly of deceiving them, but he is surprised: he believed every draenei, Broken and Lost Ones included, still remembered that they are one people.', 'quest 9803 description and reward text (they refused, choose their own path, folly of deceiving them, all part of the same people)'),
(352129, 1, 0, 255, 'At Telaar, Nahuud welcomes the one Ikuti sent. Ikuti is like a brother to him, he says, and a friend of Ikuti''s is a friend of his, and the Kurenai of Telaar give their thanks for the help shown to their people in the marsh.', 'quest 9792 reward text (Ikuti is like a brother, a friend of his is a friend of mine)'),
(352130, 1, 0, 255, 'His suspicion proved right. Plans taken from the Ango''rosh Grounds showed the ogres preparing an attack on Zabra''jin. The stench of ogres, Denjai says, always carries a threat, and now that he has proof of their intentions he means to strike before they do.', 'quest 9822 description and reward text (position can''t be an accident, attack plans, act before they do)'),
(352132, 1, 0, 255, 'In the end Fhwoor marched into the naga village by the Marshlight steam pump, lifted the Ark of Ssslith, the Bloodscale''s most prized possession, with ease, and carried it back to Sporeggar, laughing at the squishy naga. The sporelings, who saved him from the naga long ago and have had his help ever since, hope the Bloodscale will take the hint and return to their reservoir.', 'quest 9729 description and reward text (saved from the naga, stayed helping, ark, most prized possession, return to their reservoir); creature_text 17877 (lifts the Ark with ease, squishy naga)'),
(352133, 1, 0, 255, 'The Cenarion Expedition has declared a bounty on her. She is the leader of the Bloodscale naga, a sorceress last sighted at Serpent Lake, and the Expedition warns that the Bloodscale are extremely dangerous and that their leader is to be approached only with the greatest caution.', 'quest 9817 description (bounty, leader of the Bloodscale, naga sorceress, last sighted at Serpent Lake, extremely dangerous, extreme caution)'),
(352133, 2, 0, 255, 'Rajis Fyashe fell at last on the shore of Serpent Lake, struck down among the overseers and wavecallers who guarded her on the Bloodscale Grounds, and the ice and water she had turned on her foes faded with her.', 'DB spawn: Rajis Fyashe 18044 in area 3818'),
(352133, 3, 0, 255, 'Warden Hamoot called the news of her death the best he had heard all day, and paid out the Expedition''s bounty. He wagers the Bloodscale will think twice before attacking the Expedition''s scouts again.', 'quest 9817 completion and reward text (best news I''ve heard all day, think twice about attacking expedition scouts)'),
(352134, 1, 0, 255, 'The answer at Umbrafen Lake was a steam pump on the shore, worked by naga and drawing the water away. Why the naga would do such a thing, Ysiel could not guess, but it explained their open hostility toward the druids. What it did not show was how far their work reached.', 'quest 9716 reward text (the naga are behind this, but why, steam pump part of the cause, explains their open hostility); quest 9718 description (offered on turning in 9716: how widespread the naga''s activity truly is)'),
(352134, 2, 0, 255, 'To learn that, Ysiel reshaped her helper with a stormcrow amulet and sent them winging over every great lake in the marsh. The flight confirmed her fears: the naga have set up pumping stations at all the major lakes of Zangarmarsh, and they must be stopped if the marsh is to have a future.', 'quest 9718 description and reward text (Stormcrow Amulet, pumping stations at all the major lakes)'),
(352134, 3, 0, 255, 'She then handed over seeds carrying the rage of the earth, to be sown on the controls of the pumps at Umbrafen Lake, Serpent Lake, Marshlight Lake and the Lagoon. Vines as thick as an arm and as strong as iron choked the machines. The marsh was saved for now, Ysiel said, but this would not be the last of the naga.', 'quest 9720 description and reward text (Ironvine Seeds, rage of the earth, thick as your arm, strong as iron, saved for now)'),
(352135, 1, 0, 255, 'The drain is real. The naga have turned Serpent Lake into a giant water sink for the rest of the marsh, and Ysiel, who cannot guess their purpose, sent a team of druids to investigate it while she turned to other work.', 'quest 9731 reward text (giant water sink, what could they possibly be doing, team sent)'),
(352135, 2, 0, 255, 'Ysiel sent word to the Cenarion Circle as well, through its emissaries at Cenarion Post in Hellfire Peninsula. They judged the news dire and her warning wise, but help would come only when it was possible: affairs in Moonglade and Silithus have kept the Circle''s members occupied.', 'quest 9724 description and reward text (emissaries in Hellfire Peninsula, news dire, Ysiel wise); quest 9732 description (offered on turning in 9724: help as soon as possible, Moonglade and Silithus)'),
(352135, 3, 0, 255, 'Matters only grew worse. The druid team never returned from the drain, and when a search reached the entrance to Coilfang Reservoir, deep beneath the lake, it found Watcher Jhang hiding there, too badly hurt by a twisted ankle to go back for help. His companions had gone on into the reservoir without him.', 'quest 9732 reward text (matters only gotten worse); quest 9876 description and reward text (druids did not return, injuries prevented going back for help); npc_text 9112 (twisted ankle, friends inside)'),
(352136, 1, 0, 255, 'The survey turned up something alarming: the bog lords of Quagg Ridge were crossing the road to eat the sporelings'' spore pods. Leesa''oh guessed they must be starving, and though she would not normally get involved, if they kept eating the pods the sporelings would be wiped out. She sent for dietary clues from the ridge.', 'quest 9701 reward text; quest 9702 description (offered on turning in 9701: crossing the road, starving, would not normally get involved)'),
(352136, 2, 0, 255, 'Husked mushroom remains found on the ridge looked oddly familiar, and samples from the Hewn Bog to the north confirmed her hunch: Ango''rosh ogres had moved in and were cutting down the very mushrooms the bog lords fed on. Even so, Leesa''oh would not hear of wiping out the ogres, who had as much right to the marsh as anyone.', 'quest 9702 reward text (husked mushroom remains, familiar); quest 9708 description and reward text (Hewn Bog, ogres, every bit as much right)'),
(352136, 3, 0, 255, 'Instead she had boxes of harvested mushrooms taken back from the Ango''rosh Stronghold and planted them by her camp, with Buddy the cat looking on, to grow the giants a new garden. It worked, sparing the sporelings from the bog lords, and the bog lords from the Expedition''s wrath.', 'quest 9709 description and reward text (boxes of mushrooms, Ango''rosh Stronghold, new food supply); creature_text 17831 (Buddy, it''s working, saved both)'),
(352137, 1, 0, 255, 'Those who saved the sacs carried them north to Sporeggar, to the elder Msshi''fn. Protecting the next generation earned more than thanks: the sporelings, who could repay such kindness only with their hospitality, welcomed their rescuer into their homes and urged them to stay a while and meet the others, who would surely have many questions.', 'quest 9919 description (take the spore sacs to Msshi''fn in Sporeggar, north of here; they''ll be very grateful); quest 9919 reward text (protected the next generation, can only repay you by welcoming you into our homes, stay and meet the other sporelings, many questions)'),
(352137, 2, 0, 255, 'In time the sporelings answered the naga who would not leave them in peace. Their own giant, Fhwoor, led a raid on the Bloodscale by the Marshlight pump and came home with the naga''s greatest treasure, the Ark of Ssslith. If the sporelings could take that, they reasoned, worse could follow, and perhaps now the naga would go back to their reservoir.', 'quest 9729 description and reward text (Fhwoor, Ark of Ssslith, return to their reservoir)'),
(352138, 1, 0, 255, 'The Feralfen had made the ruins their own, as if they remembered something of their heritage, and Ahuurn began to hope the temple could be the key to redeeming the Lost Ones. Their idols showed a fixation on birds, though no birds live in the marsh, and he guessed they had met the arakkoa and taken them for bird spirits.', 'quest 9786 reward text (remember their heritage, key to redeeming); quest 9787 description and reward text (animal spirits, birds, arakkoa)'),
(352138, 2, 0, 255, 'So he brewed a potion to lend his envoy the shape of an arakkoa, and in that guise the envoy greeted Elder Kuruti at the temple. The elder saw through it. His people wanted nothing from the draenei who had turned their backs on them, he said, least of all a redemption offered through trickery, and he asked to be left in peace in his temple.', 'quest 9801 description (potion of arakkoa form); quest 9803 description and reward text; npc_text 9227, 9229, 9231 (Kuruti: turned their backs on us, deception, no redemption, leave my temple in peace)'),
(352138, 3, 0, 255, 'At Zabra''jin, Janidi read the captured totems. They were divided between a serpent spirit and a bird spirit, and he scorned the bird: no self-respecting Darkspear worships birds, whose spirits he calls weak and capricious and best left to the Amani. The serpent, though, wields considerable power, and that spirit he means to study.', 'quest 9846 reward text (serpent and bird, Amani, considerable power)'),
(352138, 4, 0, 255, 'Janidi coveted that power for himself. His totem, set in the ground below the Boha''mu temple stairs, called the serpent forth, and the spirit came, but it attacked, loyal to the Feralfen. Bending it to his will would cost too much, and Janidi turned to search for a new source of power in this wretched world.', 'quest 9847 description and reward text (foot of the stairs, spirit attacked, higher affinity, new source of power)'),
(352139, 1, 0, 255, 'The soil Idaar studied was nearly devoid of moisture, and if the ground itself is drying, the creatures of the mire must be suffering terribly. The pain drives the withering giants mad. They are beyond saving, Idaar judged, so the kindest course is to end their suffering.', 'quest 9782 reward text; quest 9783 description and completion text (offered on turning in 9782: devoid of moisture, pain drives them mad, beyond saving)'),
(352139, 2, 0, 255, 'Jyoba was found dead beside his spilled inkwell, his weapon still sheathed, taken by surprise as he wrote. His report was recovered from the withered giants that killed him. It said the fungal giants had gone berserk from the lack of moisture, and Zurai ordered his men to keep away: the post can afford no more losses.', 'quest 9771 reward text (inkwell, weapon sheathed, surprise); quest 9772 description and reward text (withered giants, berserk from lack of moisture, avoid the area)'),
(352139, 3, 0, 255, 'The basidium told more. Ruam at Telredor and Reavij at Swamprat Post each recognized it and knew what it meant: the Dead Mire had once been a lake like the others and the giants'' spawning ground, and with the water gone they can no longer spore. If it goes on, the giants may disappear entirely.', 'quests 9827 and 9828 descriptions and reward texts (withered basidium, once a lake, spawning ground, may disappear entirely)'),
(352139, 4, 0, 255, 'Samples from parched hydras and withered bog lords, the hardier cousins of the giants, showed the damage spreading. The drying land is taking a heavy toll on creatures never meant to live outside the swamp, and Ruam means to keep watching the mire and to consult the Cenarion Expedition on what can be done.', 'quest 10355 description and reward text (bog lords hardier cousins, heavy toll, consult the Cenarion Expedition)'),
(352140, 1, 0, 255, 'Grog''ak''s head troubled Denjai more than it pleased him. The ogres, he said, had been filtering down from the northern mountains for some time, and the position of their cutting could be no accident. Attack plans seized in the ogres'' camp to the northwest proved him right: the ogres were preparing to attack Zabra''jin, and the trolls had to act first.', 'quest 9820 reward text (filtering down from the northern mountains); quest 9822 description and reward text'),
(352140, 2, 0, 255, 'Ikuti''s call held the ogres back for the moment, but he was sure they would not give up so easily: the stubbornness of ogres is a memory that has outlasted much of his life as a draenei. The centerpiece of any ogre tribe is its leader, he says, and without one the Ango''rosh would fall to fighting over who leads next.', 'quest 9835 reward text (contained for the moment, stubbornness of the ogres); quest 9839 description (offered on turning in 9835: leader the centerpiece, infighting)'),
(352140, 3, 0, 255, 'In the stronghold Overlord Gorefist was slain with his maulers and souleaters, an example made of the overlord and his followers. Denjai celebrated the victory, but wondered aloud how long it would be before the brutes found themselves another bloodthirsty chieftain. No matter, he said: Zabra''jin will be ready for them.', 'quest 9823 description and reward text (make an example, another bloodthirsty chieftain, we''ll be ready)'),
(352140, 4, 0, 255, 'In the stronghold Overlord Gorefist was slain among his maulers, and the Kurenai''s hold on the Orebor Harborage was secured at last. Ikuti promised to send word of the deed to Telaar, and foresaw many more chances for his people and their friends to work together.', 'quest 9839 reward text (securing our position, send word to Telaar, many more opportunities)'),
(352141, 1, 0, 255, 'Morthis took the druid as his apprentice, on the condition that they do all he asks. The relics used to teach the ways of the stormcrow were entrusted long ago to an ancient druid, now deep in slumber, who must be woken. For the Ward of Waking, Morthis needs common herbs and the fragile bogblossoms that grow atop the tallest mushrooms of the marsh.', 'quest 10955 reward text (apprentice, secrets of the stormcrow, do all I ask); quest 10961 description (offered on turning in 10955: relics entrusted to an ancient druid, bogblossom)'),
(352141, 2, 0, 255, 'The relics came back from Moonglade, and with them word that troubled Morthis: he could recall no mention of outside forces tampering with the Emerald Dream, and a raven had been seen in the barrow den. He knew of a resurgent arakkoa cult in Blade''s Edge that venerates a raven god, and sent his apprentice to Arthorn Windsong at the Evergrove to learn whether the two were linked.', 'quest 10978 reward text (outside forces tampering with the Dream); quest 10979 description (offered on turning in 10978: a raven in the barrow den, raven god cult, Arthorn Windsong)'),
(352141, 3, 0, 255, 'Arthorn and the scholar Timeon had learned that a book of the raven was the cult''s ancient scripture, destroyed by arakkoa priests who held the cultists heretics. Its stone fragments, buried near Skettis, were gathered and pieced together. The Book of the Raven gave the god''s name, Anzu, and a prophecy that he would haunt the dreams of his enemies, twisting them to return to this world.', 'quest 10980 description and reward text (book of the raven, heretics, priests destroyed the holy text); quest 10988 description (raven stones buried near Skettis); creature_text 22924 (Book of the Raven, Anzu named, prophecy)'),
(352141, 4, 0, 255, 'The book also told how the raven''s followers had bound the spirits of his rivals, the eagle, the falcon and the hawk, in stone shrines under guardians, and the apprentice won back all three essences. To hold them Morthis needed a Southfury moonstone from the cliffs on the Azshara side of the river, and once it was found he set to infusing it with their power.', 'quests 10990, 10991, 10992 (shrines, guardians, essences of the eagle, falcon and hawk); quest 10994 description and reward text (Southfury moonstone, Azshara, infusing it)'),
(352141, 5, 0, 255, 'In the Sethekk Halls the moonstone was set in the raven''s claw before the talon king''s hall, so that Anzu would believe his followers had gathered to welcome him back. The raven god came forth from the Emerald Dream and was defeated, and Morthis declared that victory worth more than any test or rite of passage he could set.', 'quest 11001 description and reward text (raven''s claw, lure Anzu from the Emerald Dream, more than any test or rite of passage)'),
(352141, 6, 0, 255, 'Yet Morthis fears Anzu may not abandon his quest to return. As long as the raven god has followers in Outland he will try to rise again, so Morthis bids his student keep the essence-infused moonstone, ready to defeat him once more should he gather his strength.', 'quest 11011 description and reward text (may not abandon his quest, followers, keep the moonstone)');
